/*! \page IO_intro Input, output and orchestration

\section IO_intro_introduction Introduction

A run is driven from Python by the class \ref py_utils::simulation::RadClusterSimulation "RadClusterSimulation" in radcluster_code/py_utils/simulation.py. The class loads the inputs, builds the rate constants and the material graph, starts the C++ solver, and writes a timestamped output directory.

\verbatim
from radcluster_code.py_utils.simulation import RadClusterSimulation

sim = RadClusterSimulation(
    I=1000, V=1000,
    solver_mode='full_system',
    equations='bin_moment',
    cascade='fusion',
    he_kinetics='quasi_steady_state',
    i_mobile=5, v_mobile=2,
)

results = sim.run(solver_config={
    't_span': (1e-6, 1e8),
    'n_points': 300,
    'log_time': True,
    'rtol': 1e-6, 'atol': 1e-20,
    'solver_method': {'linsol': 'gmres', 'preconditioner': 'Woodbury'},
})
\endverbatim

The driver notebook radcluster_code/codes/Notebooks/RadCluster_2_1.ipynb documents every control variable, builds the solver if needed, runs the case, and prints the end-of-run summary.

\section IO_intro_pages Pages

